# play logs ----------------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode, mocks: the Logs screen of slice 1, inferred from$
# v0.3.2 and origin/main, read from a simulated host by the real$
# reader (pkg/engine/logview), its rows and layout unit (c)'s to$
# build. It only reads: no plan, no y/N, no journal. No pager$
# runs: an item says what it would run. Nothing on this machine$
# changes: every command and file is the fake's.$
$
# Logs hosts ###################################################$
$
  Select a host$
$
   1) A log with lines     Fits the screen$
   2) A long log           1204 lines$
   3) No log yet           No file$
   4) Unreadable           A directory there$
   5) Empty                No lines$
   6) Control characters   Escape sequences, shown safe$
   7) logFile elsewhere    hardn.yml says another path$
   8) Alpine 3.23          BusyBox's less$
   9) No pager             No less installed$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter your choice [0-9 or q]: 6$
$
# Info: logs/control$
# web-01.example.net runs Debian 13, less installed. Lines hold$
# what commands printed: colour, a title and bell, a bidi$
# override, bytes that are not UTF-8, typographic characters.$
# Those a terminal would act on show as ^[ and <U+202E> and$
# <0xe9>, the rest as they are, in either glyph set; origin/main$
# prints them raw to the terminal (logging.go:146;$
# file_logs_repository.go:96; menu/logs_escape.golden).$
$
